(1, 'admin', 'psa.acacongress2025@gmail.com', NULL, '$2y$12$IxKq60hSD9R54RYLm5z1IudkMJ17KvkC8R3TsoLx1oML7MtyprxKG', NULL, NULL, NULL, 'rEJElg66m8oM6FTwC9GKNSLbERoBV52f15olUcx67a2tX92wqw7pkssnyfdM', 1, NULL, '2025-01-20 16:27:14', '2025-06-03 15:26:57', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 'admin'),
(2, 'Paul Reyes', 'pcreyes09@gmail.com', NULL, '$2y$12$dGCNzp0.O6SpPlysw0uwZOwrg.2KI3UpCwFIOGyNKyxPQBM3GklPq', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, '2025-02-10 15:05:18', '2025-02-19 10:00:41', 'Paul Cedrick Reyes', 'Philippines', 'Philippine General Hospital', 'Ermita, Manila', 'Lorem Ipsum is simply dummy text of the printing and typesetting industry. Lorem Ipsum has been the industry\'s standard dummy text ever since the 1500s, when an unknown printer took a galley of type and scrambled it to make a type specimen book. It has survived not only five centuries, but also the leap into electronic typesetting, remaining essentially unchanged. It was popularised in the 1960s with the release of Letraset sheets containing Lorem Ipsum passages, and more recently with desktop publishing software like Aldus PageMaker including versions of Lorem Ipsum.\n\nLorem Ipsum is simply dummy text of the printing and typesetting industry. Lorem Ipsum has been the industry\'s standard dummy text ever since the 1500s, when an unknown printer took a galley of type and scrambled it to make a type specimen book. It has survived not only five centuries, but also the leap into electronic typesetting, remaining essentially unchanged. It was popularised in the 1960s with the release of Letraset sheets containing Lorem Ipsum passages, and more recently with desktop publishing software like Aldus PageMaker including versions of Lorem Ipsum.\n\nLorem Ipsum is simply dummy text of the printing and typesetting industry. Lorem Ipsum has been the industry\'s standard dummy text ever since the 1500s, when an unknown printer took a galley of type and scrambled it to make a type specimen book. It has survived not only five centuries, but also the leap into electronic typesetting, remaining essentially unchanged. It was popularised in the 1960s with the release of Letraset sheets containing Lorem Ipsum passages, and more recently with desktop publishing software like Aldus PageMaker including versions of Lorem Ipsum.\n\nLorem Ipsum is simply dummy text of the printing and typesetting industry. Lorem Ipsum has been the industry\'s standard dummy text ever since the 1500s until today.', 'Paul Cedrick Reyes Philippines 021925.jpg', '09214048218', 'test'),
(44, 'pen cano', 'pencano@yahoo.com', NULL, '$2y$12$yJG4h32HQ2r8qUBnYWMAne2yOt2dw6vgfFdr2wgBJQ8tDYzghkNCW', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, '2025-02-14 13:52:52', '2025-02-14 13:52:52', 'pen cano', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 'test'),
(45, 'Penafrancia Cano', 'pencanoasian@gmail.com', NULL, '$2y$12$lqHa6fcTQa.8TYkGB/xfVuZqBML5VPw/it4yIgf1R3RCSEqCNHqou', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, '2025-02-15 14:36:15', '2025-02-15 14:40:44', 'Penafrancia Cano', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 'test'),
(46, 'JINTAE Kim', 'jintae73@gmail.com', NULL, '$2y$12$jrTM6LwR1F0c8TQB4kGiZ.xPzioJHmE10siqA55R6wXP6o3UtyZMu', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, '2025-02-19 12:02:43', '2025-03-27 12:36:40', 'JINTAE Kim', 'South Korea', 'Seoul National University | South Korea', 'Anesthesiolgy Dept, SNUH, Daehakro101, Seoul, South Korea', 'Dr. Jin-Tae Kim is the Professor of Department of Anesthesiology and Pain Medicine at Seoul National University College of Medicine. He graduated from Seoul National University College of Medicine in 1998. He finished his internship in 1999 and resident training in 2003 at Seoul National University Hospital. He completed post-doctoral research fellowship at Duke University Hospital in the US. His major field of clinical and research interest is perioperative medicine. Subspecialties are pediatric anesthesia, cardiac anesthesia and regional anesthesia. He is currently a director of academic affairs of KSA,  president of KSRA, a immediate past president of KSPA, and a director of planning of KSCVA. He performed many clinical and basic research regarding perioperative medicine, practical ultrasonography and acute pain management. He published more than 330 peer-reviewed journal articles.', 'JINTAE Kim SOUTH KOERA 021925.jpg', '01062608490', 'speaker'),
(47, 'Tony Ng', 'tonyktng@gmail.com', NULL, '$2y$12$PwWqo/1wlwH6fSMkdty/Q.q6aKYuFRsDoemS5Np.EeS4kS28kyT7O', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, '2025-02-19 13:52:04', '2025-10-23 14:18:05', 'Tony Ng', 'Australia/Hong Kong', 'Concord Repatriation General Hospital, Sydney; Sydney Pain Management Centre | Australia', 'Sydney, Australia/Shatin, Hong Kong', 'Dr. Ng is a dual specialist in both anaesthesiology and pain medicine in Hong Kong and Australia. \n\nDual FIPP and CIPS qualifications from World Institute of Pain.  \n\nAwardee of the Hong Kong Academy of Medicine (HKAM) Distinguished Young Fellow in Anaesthesiology in 2015.\n\nCurrently:\n1. Specialist anaesthetist and Pain medicine physician, Sydney Pain Management Centre, Sydney, Australia\n2. Consultant Pain Medicine physician, Concord Repatriaion General Hospital, Sydney, Australia \n3. Honorary Clinical Associate Professor, Department of Anaesthesia and intensive care, the Chinese University of Hong Kong. \n\n\n He also serves as: \n1. Educational Committee member, NYSORA\n2. Board member in Board of Pain Medicine (Hong Kong College of Anaesthesiologists)\n3. Council member, Hong Kong Pain Society\n4. Research Committee member, Faculty of Pain Medicine, ANZCA\n\nInvolved in multiple book and journal publications on ultrasound-guided pain intervention and regional block, regenerative medicine and chemical denervation of peripheral joints.\n\nCurrent journal reviewer of multiple international journals, such as Regional Anesthesia and Pain Medicine,  and Anaesthesia.', 'Tony Ng Australia-Hong Kong 021925.jpg', '+61 0483152349/ +852 96703034', 'speaker'),
(48, 'Hasmizy Muhammad', 'hasmizymuhammad@gmail.com', NULL, '$2y$12$Nsi5W.dm5TyllxRHNG365eNw.nANozaNm7qG2eLQBceiwiK0wpQe2', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, '2025-02-19 14:15:06', '2025-02-19 15:26:16', 'Hasmizy Muhammad', 'Malaysia', 'Sarawak Heart Centre | Malaysia', 'Department of Anaesthesiology and Critical Care, Sarawak Heart Centre, 94300, Kota Samarahan, Sarawak', 'Dr. Hasmizy Muhammad is a Senior Consultant Cardiothoracic Anaesthesiologist and Head of the Department of Anaesthesiology and Critical Care at Sarawak Heart Centre, Malaysia. He is also Head of Subspecialty Cardiothoracic Anaesthesiology and Perfusion, and Head of Training, Parallel Pathway Specialist Training for Anaesthesiology and Critical Care at the Ministry of Health Malaysia.\n\nDr. Hasmizy Muhammad received a medical degree in 1998 and Master of Medicine (Anaesthesiology) in 2006 from University Science Malaysia. He was trained in cardiac anaesthesia and perfusion at Sarawak General Hospital in 2008 and Konkuk University Medical Centre, Seoul, South Korea, in 2011. He obtained a Graduate Diploma in Clinical Ultrasound from University of Melbourne in 2016, Master in Business Administration from University Tun Abdul Razak in 2022, Leadership in Medicine: Southeast Asia Certificate Program from Harvard Medical School in 2023, and gained experience in ECMO at the University Hospital Regensburg (Germany) and paediatrics cardiac anaesthesia at the Royal Brompton Hospital (UK).\n\nDr. Hasmizy Muhammad holds leadership positions in societies as President-Elect of the Malaysian Society of Anaesthesiologists (MSA), Honorary Secretary of the College of Anaesthesiologists, Academy of Medicine of Malaysia, Vice President of the Malaysian Cardiothoracic Anaesthesiology and Perfusion Society (MASCAP), and Chairman of the Sarawak Perfusion Society.\n\nDr. Hasmizy Muhammad is actively involved in teaching and training in anesthesiology, perfusion, and echocardiography. He is an examiner for the Master of Anaesthesiology and Critical Care conducted by Malaysia Conjoint Board of Examination of Anaesthesiology and Critical Care,  and Fellowship of The College of Anaesthesiologists of Ireland.', 'Hasmizy Muhammad Malaysia 021925.jpg', '60138067966', 'speaker'),
(49, 'Suraphong Lorsomradee', 'slorsomr@gmail.com', NULL, '$2y$12$P4mubOs0Dqo3ME8SwT39eeb0MXp7.IVMxc32TWygb601Z2KoHzsr2', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, '2025-02-19 15:05:04', '2025-02-19 15:08:11', 'Suraphong Lorsomradee', 'Thailand', 'Chiang Mai University Hospital | Thailand', NULL, 'Suraphong Lorsomradee, MD., PhD., is the Asia representative of the Council of World Federation of Societies of Anesthesiologists (WFSA Council), Deputy Dean of Multidisciplinary School of Chiang Mai University, associated professor, head of division of cardiac anesthesia, TIVA Training Center, Faculty of Medicine, Chiang Mai University Hospital. THAILAND.\n\nHe is the scientific chairman of the Society of Cardiothoracic and Vascular Anesthesiologists of Thailand (SCAT), Board of Directors of Asia Anesthesia Forum (AAF), and Board of Directors of Asian Society of Cardiothoracic Anesthesia (ASCA), and Board of the World Society of Intravenous Anesthesia (WSIVA).\n\nHe is an international educator of anesthesia and critical care medicine in Asia, especially IV anesthesia, simulation, practical fluid and hemodynamic management (GDTEducAsia). He completed the fellowship in cardiac anesthesia and transplantation anesthesia from Antwerp University Hospital, Belgium. His PhD in medicine from Keio University Tokyo Japan was in cardiac output and hemodynamic monitoring, and his current research interests include hemodynamic monitoring,  ERAS and functional recovery after surgery.', 'Suraphong Lorsomradee Thailand 021925.jpg', '+66861972167', 'speaker'),
(50, 'Xavier Falieres', 'x.falieres@gmail.com', NULL, '$2y$12$iR744tCqs2r4KnbMY0Ib9e5sPm/ga2Hz3htNVskz1980VBLwKliIi', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, '2025-02-20 17:33:53', '2025-02-20 17:45:53', 'Xavier Falieres', 'Netherlands', 'Albert Schweitzer Hospital | Netherlands', NULL, 'Xavier Falieres was born on August 18, 1963, in France. He studied general and emergency medicine in France.\n\nIn 1993, he moved to Belgium to pursue studies in anesthesiology and intensive care. Later, he settled in the Netherlands, where he has been working as a perioperative anesthesiologist since 2002 at the Albert Schweitzer Hospital and the Helene Schweitzer Clinic, a major teaching hospital near Rotterdam.\n\nHe also earned a degree in hospital medical management in the Netherlands.\nXavier served as the medical director of the operating theater for 12 years. He is a board member of the Ambulatory and Short-Stay Department.\n\nCurrently, he is the president of the Dutch Society for Ambulatory Care and Short Stay (NVDK) and a member of the Management Body of the International Association for Ambulatory Surgery (IAAS). Within IAAS, his role is to assist countries aiming to develop ambulatory surgery programs.\n\nHe frequently teaches and conducts workshops in developing countries.\n\nHis primary areas of interest in anesthesiology include techniques for ambulatory surgery, opioid-reduced anesthesia, loco-regional anesthesia, thoracic surgery, obstetrics, anesthesia for geriatric patients, and orthopedic surgery. \n\nHe is part of the ERATS (Enhanced Recovery After Thoracic Surgery) project in the Netherlands.\n\nIn management, his focus is primarily on ambulatory surgery units and improving patient safety throughout the perioperative process.\n\nXavier’s hobbies include traveling, classical music, and serving as a board member of the association Français des Pays-Bas, which helps French expatriates settle in the Netherlands.', 'Xavier Falieres Netherlands 022025.jpg', NULL, 'speaker'),
(51, 'ErHlDStuzBcs', 'oybrinj@gmail.com', NULL, '$2y$12$yTtb9CMlCFpzq6qvuzTuB.y4yFaB2S8ek8HCKStYEgutFvvkBXyiS', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, '2025-02-20 20:08:17', '2025-02-20 20:08:17', 'ErHlDStuzBcs', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 'unknown'),
(52, 'Christopher Bowden', 'bowdencc@hotmail.com', NULL, '$2y$12$9fqB9wL0XkAAZ2bu20LaP.tYcebMuiuqv8Tg0ez1bj44tg61Qki.6', NULL, NULL, NULL, 'hBTeeDBoim4UOSMh7amqfbCbJDIck8eWNHVIArkNoJzBqznNHulSh4bGrIJL', NULL, NULL, '2025-02-21 05:38:59', '2025-02-21 05:42:34', 'Christopher Bowden', 'Australia', 'Gold Coast University Hospital | Australia', NULL, 'Dr Chris Bowden has worked as a consultant anaesthetist in Australia for the last 20 years and is currently Deputy Director of the Anaesthetic Department at the Gold Coast University Hospital in Queensland, Australia.\n\nHe has worked and taught throughout the Pacific region and has held academic roles at the Fiji National University, including Adjunct Professor in Anaesthesia. He is the immediate Past Chair of the Australian Society of Anaesthetists Overseas Development and Education Committee and is a Final Examiner of the Australian and New Zealand College of Anaesthetists.\n\nHe is the current Chair of the Asian Australasian Regional Section of the WFSA and is a member of the WFSA Council. Areas of interest include leadership development, professional wellbeing and education, and he has presented at many national and international Anaesthesia meetings.', 'Christopher Bowden Australia 022125.jpg', NULL, 'speaker'),
(53, 'Vesna Jevtovic-Todorovic', 'vesna.jevtovic-todorovic@cuanschutz.edu', NULL, '$2y$12$khERt0MuedGk.NVuSeV4KuAeITqkfkc8J2btfncoB0LI9oGxNmsNa', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, '2025-02-21 07:52:54', '2025-02-21 08:01:41', 'Vesna Jevtovic-Todorovic', 'United States', 'University of Colorado Hospital School of Medicine | USA', '12401 E 17th Ave, MS B113, Aurora, CO 80045', 'Vesna Todorovic is the inaugural CU Medicine Endowed Chair and Chair of the Department of Anesthesiology at the University of Colorado School of Medicine.  Dr. Todorovic received her graduate education at the University of Belgrade in Serbia (MD) and the University of Illinois, Chicago (PhD) and completed residency training in Anesthesia at the Washington University School of Medicine in St. Louis.  She earned an MBA from the University of Virginia, Charlottesville, VA and received the Harold Carron Professor of Anesthesiology Endowment from the University of Virginia Health System.  \n\nDr. Todorovic is a practicing anesthesiologist working simultaneously as a clinician scientist for over 26 years.  Dr. Todorovic has developed three major lines of research:  anesthetics as neurotoxins, management of chronic pain and mechanisms of anesthesia-induced developmental neurodegeneration which are federally funded resulting in over 140 peer-reviewed publications and 11 patents.  She has received numerous grants from organizations such as the National Institutes of Health, March of Dimes, the American Heart Association and the American Diabetes Association.\n\nDr. Todorovic served as the Chair of the National Institutes of Health’s Surgery, Anesthesiology and Trauma study section.  She serves on the Editorial Board for the Journal of Neurosurgical Anesthesiology and the Associate Editorial Board for British Journal of Anaesthesia.  In addition, she serves as an Associate Editor for Anesthesiology.  \n\nIn her role as a PI, Dr. Todorovic has mentored and trained over 60 graduate students, medical students and post-docs.  As Chair, her focus extends to the mentorship and growth of junior faculty, expanding clinical programs and increasing collaboration with the School of Medicine and the surrounding community. \n', 'Vesna Jevtovic-Todorovic United States 022125.jpg', '43434095054', 'speaker'),
(58, 'Sophia Chew', 'sthchew@gmail.com', NULL, '$2y$12$i9tIdSp0d..1BVmO/vVdcOfSBzgru0y/3j7AugbQ6zHsYpBDOM7/O', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, '2025-02-21 10:06:42', '2025-02-21 10:22:05', 'Sophia Chew', 'Singapore', 'Singapore General Hospital', 'Outram Road S169608', 'Qualifications:      MBBS, MMED, FANZCA, FAMS\nPosition:                Senior Consultant, Department of Anaesthesiology, Singapore General \n                                 Hospital\nOther Affiliation: Clinical Associate Professor, Yong Loo Lin School of Medicine, National \n                                  University of Singapore\n          		                  Clinical Associate Professor, Duke-NUS Medical School\n		                          Honorary Clinical Associate Professor, Department of Anaesthesiology, \n                                  School of  Clinical Medicine, Hong Kong University\n         \nEmail :                  Sophia.chew.t.h@singhealth.com.sg\nNo :                       63214220\nFax :                      62241792\n\nBiography\nA/Prof Sophia Chew obtained her MBBS from the National University of Singapore and subsequently trained to be an anesthesiologist.  She obtained the MMED(Anaesthesia) from the National University of Singapore and the Fellowship of the Australian and New Zealand College of Anaesthestists (FANZCA).  She did a fellowship training in cardiac anaesthesia at the Duke University Medical Centre in the United States of America.\nA/Prof Chew currently practises at the Singapore General Hospital and is the Director of Research at the Division of Anaesthesiology and Perioperative Medicine.  She is also the Academic Deputy Vice-Chair, Research, SingHealth Duke-NUS Anaesthesiology and Perioperative Sciences Academic Clinical Programme.  Her research interests include safety outcomes after cardiac surgery, airway management, aging and perioperative medicine.  She has received several grants, both local and international for research and numerous awards for her research and education endeavours.  A/Prof Chew has also published several peer reviewed papers in highly acclaimed journals.  \nA/Prof Chew is the Assistant Master, Academy of Medicine, Singapore and the immediate Past President, Singapore Society of Anaesthesiologists.  As President of the SSA, she co organised the successful World Congress of Anaesthesiologists 2024 in Singapore.  A/Prof Chew previously served as the President, College of Anaesthesiologists and chaired the Sedation Guidelines Committee, Ministry of Health, Singapore.\n', 'Sophia Chew Singapore 022125.jpg', '98203670', 'speaker'),
(60, 'Bishwas Pradhan', 'biswaspradhan@yahoo.com', NULL, '$2y$12$70H.dUG/aB40YimUD3pnu.y/ctok.nhvFwWBTozZmG83ng1F0cBDW', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, '2025-02-21 11:16:38', '2025-02-21 11:45:30', 'Bishwas Pradhan', 'Nepal', 'Manmohan Cardiothoracic Vascular & Transplant Center, Kathmandu Nepal', 'Maharajgunj, Kathmandu, Nepal', '\nCURRICULUM VITAE\n\nProf. Dr. Bishwas Pradhan, MD \n(Fellowship – Cardiothoracic Anesthesia & Critical Care)\n\n\n\n1)	Name				:	BISHWAS PRADHAN\n\n2)	Date of Birth			:	25th April 1972 AD \n\n3)	Nationality			:	Nepali\n\n5)	Current Address		: 	Budhanilkantha - 4, Kathmandu, Nepal\n\n6)	Contacts			:	 Mobile – 00977 - 9851068669,  E mail – biswaspradhan@yahoo.com\n                                                                               \n7. Current designation:\n\nProfessor& Head,\nDepartment of Cardiothoracic & Vascular Anesthesiology, MCVTC, MMC, IOM, TU\n\n\n8.  Academic Roles (Teacher/Guide/Examiner) for:\n•	MBBS\n•	MD Anesthesiology program\n•	DM (Ph. D level) Critical care Medicine program\n\n\n 9. Instructor\n•	AHA, ACLS course\n•	Coordinator, CPR program – IOM, Nepal\n     NYSORA USA, March 2, 3 2014\n\n10. Topics of interest:\n•	Antibiotic stewardship\n•	ECMO\n•	Hemodynamic monitoring\n•	Airway management\n•	Patient blood management \n•	Anticoagulation & Regional Anesthesia\n\n\n11. Membership of  Societies:	\n\nI.	Nepal Medical Council\nII.	Nepal Medical Association \nIII.	 Member – \n•	SCA, USA\n•	Nepalese Society of Critical Care Medicine\n•	Cardiac Society of Nepal\n•	IARS, USA\n\nIV.	Society of Anesthesiologists of Nepal (SAN),\n•	President, SAN, 2017 March  – 2019 March\n•	Organising Secretary 11th  & 12th SAN Conference, 2010 & 2011\n•	Organising President, 19th & 20th SANCON, 2018 & 2019\n\nV.	Founder Editor in Chief,\n•	Journal of Society of Anesthesiologists of Nepal\n\n12. Publications/Academic participation:\n\n•	41 in National & International Journals.\n•	Invited as Faculty in National & International Conferences\n\n13. Milestones:\n        \n•	First beating heart CABG surgery in Nepal\n•	First Renal transplantation in Nepal\n•	Introduction in Nepal\n           o	Intraoperative TEE \n           o	Point of Care Coagulation System\n           o	Autologous Blood Transfusion System  \n           o	Nitric Oxide ', 'Bishwas Pradhan Nepal 022125.jpg', '+9779851068669', 'speaker'),
(89, 'URxMtMotoSbw', 'lindsimeg75@gmail.com', NULL, '$2y$12$kY3Luf.Lk6NIad3K7.XPXO7EQTN2gAmDA.e/piJYISBLPIDpBLeSK', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, '2025-02-22 23:19:15', '2025-02-22 23:19:15', 'URxMtMotoSbw', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 'unknown'),
(93, 'Samuel Ern Hung Tsan', 'samuel.tsan@gmail.com', NULL, '$2y$12$BwEj7UsF0D0SddZRVFruMOOCKxdAkvoXSCXQ3i5eegOVahCVNqO/O', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, '2025-02-24 10:46:06', '2025-02-24 11:43:46', 'Samuel Ern Hung Tsan', 'Malaysia', 'University of Malaysia Sarawak | Malaysia', 'Jalan Datuk Mohd Musa, 94300 Kota Samarahan, Sarawak.', 'Dr Samuel Ern Hung Tsan is a consultant neuroanaesthesiologist and neurointensivist at the University of Malaysia Sarawak and Sarawak General Hospital. \n\nHe holds a Master of Anaesthesiology with Distinction from the University of Malaya and is a Fellow of the College of Anaesthesiologists of Ireland. He completed his International College on Perioperative Neurosciences Training-accredited neuroanaesthesiology and neurointensive care fellowships at St George’s Hospital in London, United Kingdom. \n\nHe is a dedicated researcher who, in addition to authoring publications in international peer-reviewed journals, has contributed multiple book chapters. His research interests include regional anaesthesia in neurosurgery, neurointensive care, airway management, and physician mental health. He is actively engaged in teaching undergraduate medical students and postgraduate anaesthesiology trainees. He refines his clinical practice at Sarawak General Hospital, where he provides specialized neuroanesthesia and neurointensive care services. His current leadership roles include serving as an executive committee member of the Malaysian Society of Anaesthesiologists and as the Convenor for the Wellbeing Special Interest Group in the College of Anaesthesiologists, Academy of Medicine, Malaysia. \n', 'Samuel Ern Hung Tsan Malaysia 022425.jpg', '+60108040711', 'speaker'),
(97, 'Heather Nixon', 'hnixon1@uic.edu', NULL, '$2y$12$PLO4.5UxeyTq4cnJA5Cv9OvUa9ot9P4lbb2WhRHBpL8l2/TpCiPdS', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, '2025-07-25 22:56:59', '2025-07-25 22:58:30', 'Heather Nixon', 'United States of America', 'University of Illinois At Chicago Hospital | USA', '1740 W. Taylor Street, Suite 3200,  Chicago  IL 60612', 'Dr. Heather Nixon is a Professor of Anesthesiology and the Division Chief of Obstetric Anesthesiology at the University of Illinois Hospital at Chicago where she has worked for the last 13 years. \nShe completed her residency at the University of Illinois at Chicago Medical School and her Obstetric Anesthesiology Fellowship at Northwestern Memorial Hospital – Feinberg School of Medicine.  Her previous academic appointments include Residency Program Director, Associate Head for Education and Obstetric Anesthesiology Fellowship Director.    Dr. Nixon served on the Illinois Maternal Mortality Review Committee for 6 years.\nNationally, she served as the Vice Chair for the American Society of Anesthesiologists Committee on Obstetric Anesthesia for six years and a member of the board of directors for the Society of Obstetric Anesthesia and Perinatology for the last 10 years.  Heather is the current Immediate President of the Society of Obstetric Anesthesia and Perinatology.  She is a recognized national and international speaker and is a passionate advocate for patient safety as it relates to medication management in anesthesiology and the patient experience in obstetric anesthesia care.  Notably, she is featured in the New York Time and Serial Productions “The Retrievals Season 2” for her quality improvement and safety work in the clinical area of intraoperative pain during cesarean delivery. \n', 'Heather Nixon United States of America 072525.jpg', '7736159419', 'speaker'),
(108, 'Annery Garcia-Marcinkiewicz', 'dstiedemann@example.com', NULL, '$2y$12$O0U9GmdP3BXrUUqNgKOCFOWiSxc9ufhJKIklQv66RqPWOqmkVOBqC', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, '2025-02-24 13:20:56', '2025-02-24 13:20:56', 'Annery Garcia-Marcinkiewicz', 'USA', 'Children’s Hospital of Philadelphia | USA', NULL, 'Annery Garcia-Marcinkiewicz, MD, MSCE, is an Associate Professor of Anesthesiology and Critical Care at the Children’s Hospital of Philadelphia (CHOP), University of Pennsylvania. She is an Associate Division Chief for General Anesthesiology, and the Director of the Difficult Airway Program at CHOP. Dr. Garcia-Marcinkiewicz is passionate about improving the safety of pediatric airway management and airway education. She is the site PI for the Pediatric Difficult Intubation Registry at CHOP and enjoys engaging other interested sites in performing airway research.  Dr. Garcia-Marcinkiewicz serves on the board of Women in Anesthesiology and is the current President. \n\nDr. Garcia-Marcinkiewicz received her undergraduate degree from the Sophie Davis School of Biomedical Education, at the City University of New York, where she studied biomedical science. She graduated from the New York University School of Medicine and completed her Anesthesiology residency at Mayo Clinic in Rochester, Minnesota in 2015. Dr. Garcia-Marcinkiewicz then did her pediatric anesthesiology fellowship at CHOP and remained on faculty since 2016. She then obtained a Master of Science in Clinical Epidemiology from the University of Pennsylvania in 2021. Her current focus is the development of an Airway education and research lab called the Pediatric Center for Airway Research, “PCAR”. ', 'Annery Garcia-Marcinkiewicz 091125.jpg', NULL, 'speaker'),
(115, 'Ina Ismiarti Shariffuddin', 'inashariffuddin@gmail.com', NULL, '$2y$12$VQ2u5jACbZveHsQQhT166uVJyQvSWedvBw8mmb924.hbXGKzz62SC', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, '2025-08-06 19:34:32', '2025-08-19 09:52:25', 'Ina Ismiarti Shariffuddin', 'Malaysia', 'University Malaya Medical Centre | Malaysia', 'Kuala Lumpur, Malaysia', 'Dr Ina Ismiarti Shariffuddin is Professor and Senior Consultant Anaesthesiologist at the Faculty of Medicine, Universiti Malaya. She obtained her MBChB from the University of Dundee, a Master of Anaesthesiology and a Master in Medical Education (Distinction) from Universiti Malaya, Fellowships in Paediatric Anaesthesia from KK Women\'s and Children\'s Hospital, Singapore, and certification in Paediatric Liver Transplantation from Renji Hospital, Shanghai Jiao Tong University, China.\nDr. Ina is a strong advocate for perioperative patient blood management, sustainable anaesthesia, and advanced airway management and patient safety.  Her leadership includes presidencies of the College of Anaesthesiologists, Academy of Medicine Malaysia, Malaysia Society of Anaesthesiologists, and Malaysian Paediatric Society of Anaesthesiologists. She is the current President Elect for the Asian Society of Paediatric Anaesthesiologists and a member of the task force appointed by WFSA to develop its inaugural Leadership Module. During COVID-19, she led the Anaesthesiology and Intensive Care Department at Universiti Malaya Medical Centre.\nProfessor Dr. Ina has been an invited speaker in many prestigious international and national scientific conferences, sharing her expertise in perioperative management of paediatric patients, advanced airway management in anaesthesia and acute care, patient blood management, medical education, sustainability and leadership. Her contributions to the scientific community are well-documented through her publication in esteemed international peer-reviewed journals. \nHer pioneering work in Basic Life Support education earned her the “Ronald Harden  Innovation in Medical Education” and “Rogayah Jaafar Innovation in Health Professions Education” Awards in 2024. She holds two patents and one copyright in Anaesthesia and Critical Care, underscoring her commitment to patient safety and innovation. She currently serves as Chief Editor of the Malaysian Journal of Anaesthesiology.\n', 'ina Ismiarti Shariffuddin malaysia 080625.jpg', '+60122353134', 'speaker'),
(125, 'Balavenkat Subramanian', 'demario.marquardt@example.net', NULL, '$2y$12$O0U9GmdP3BXrUUqNgKOCFOWiSxc9ufhJKIklQv66RqPWOqmkVOBqC', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, '3', '2025-02-24 13:20:56', '2025-02-24 13:20:56', 'Balavenkat Subramanian', 'India', 'Ganga Medical Centre & Hospitals Pvt. Ltd. | India', NULL, 'Rtn. Dr J. Balavenkata Subramanian, MD, DA\nSenior Consultant & Academic Director,\nDepartment of Anaesthesia & Perioperative Care\nGanga Medical Centre & Hospitals Pvt. Ltd.\n\nSecretary -  World Federation of Society of Anaesthesiologists 2024-2026\nPresident - Indian Society of Anaesthesiologists 2024 - 2025\nImmediate Past President - Asian Oceanic Society of Regional Anaesthesia\nEducational Committee Member - World Federation of Society of Anaesthesiologists 2020-2026\nNational Chairman - Academy of Regional Anaesthesia” of India\nMember - ASRAPM Newsletter Committee\nCourse Director - \nAeasculap Academy Ganga Hospital Regional Anaesthesia Guidance Centre\nWFSA - GANGA Hospital Regional Anaesthesia Fellowship\nPost Doctoral Fellowship in Nerve Block and Pain Management - Dr MGR Medical University', 'Balavenkat Subramanian 091825.jpg', NULL, 'speaker'),
(126, 'Alex Sia Tiong Heng', 'alex.sia.t.h@singhealth.com.sg', NULL, '$2y$12$Ge2oJ61dtL0W33nsKIgyT.m4nQXJrdhYg6XBOiaHTGbyq48An.KUK', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, '2025-02-24 15:31:53', '2025-02-24 15:33:58', 'Alex Sia Tiong Heng', 'Singapore', 'KK Women\'s & Children\'s Hospital | Singapore', '100 Bukit Timah Road, Singapore 229899', 'Prof Alex Sia has been CEO of KKH since May 2017, leading it as a key National Centre for women and children\'s health and a global Academic Medical Centre. Under his leadership, KKH has formed numerous international and national partnerships, notably establishing the Maternal and Child Health Research Institute, which has strengthened its research impact through competitive funding, high-impact publications, and improved clinical care. He also spearheaded the KKH Offices for Population and Global Health, enhancing KKH’s influence and reach. In 2024, KKH was ranked the 9th Best Children’s Hospital in the Asia-Pacific region by Newsweek-Statista and achieved its highest ranking (30th overall, 2nd in healthcare) in Singapore’s Top 100 Best Employers by Straits Times-Statista.\n\nProf Sia has driven advancements in patient safety and medication administration through automation, holding three SingHealth-owned patents granted by the USPTO. He co-founded two med-tech startups, including HiCURA Pte Ltd, which developed the first AI-powered ultrasound-guided system for neuraxial blocks and was listed by Forbes Asia as a ‘Top 100 New Company to Watch’ in 2022. His research includes pharmacogenomics of pain and opioid use, with over 150 peer-reviewed articles, multiple book chapters, and two edited textbooks. His H-index is 51, ranking first in ‘Obstetric Anaesthesia’ on Google Scholar. A Harvard study recognized his work on labour epidural analgesia as a top publication in obstetric anesthesiology. In 2024, Stanford University and Elsevier named him among the ‘World’s Top 2% Most Cited Scientists’ for career-long research impact.', 'Alex Sia Tiong Heng Singapore 022425.jpg', '+6590609831', 'speaker'),
(127, 'Azarinah Izaham', 'azaizaham@hctm.ukm.edu.my', NULL, '$2y$12$JttLFHbeqwyniLok.xNyh.jM5NHKcejR3IyOPg0APMeFwHBmFHc06', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, '2025-02-25 08:07:15', '2025-02-25 08:12:14', 'Azarinah Izaham', 'Malaysia', 'Universiti Kebangsaan Malaysia', 'Bandar Tun Razak, Kuala Lumpur, Malaysia', 'Dr. Azarinah Izaham is an Associate Professor and Consultant Anaesthesiologist at the Faculty of Medicine, Universiti Kebangsaan Malaysia (UKM) in Kuala Lumpur. After obtaining her medical degree from UKM in 1999, she completed her postgraduate specialization in anaesthesiology at the same institution in 2007.\n\nWith extensive experience across various disciplines in anaesthesiology and critical care, she specializes in perioperative management for liver surgery & transplantation, and endocrine surgery. Dr. Azarinah plays a pivotal role in medical education, training undergraduate and postgraduate medical students, nurses, medical technologists, and paramedical practitioners in medicine and anaesthesiology.\n\nAs an established examiner for the Board of Examination of Anaesthesiology & Intensive Care in Malaysia, she has contributed significantly to maintaining professional standards in the field. Her academic contributions include numerous publications in both local and international peer-reviewed journals.\n\nCurrently, Dr. Azarinah serves in several leadership positions: Head of Department of Anaesthesiology & Intensive Care at UKM\'s Faculty of Medicine, Chair of the Specialty Committee of Anaesthesiology Malaysia, and Honorary Secretary of the Malaysian Society of Anaesthesiologists. Through these roles, she continues to shape the future of anaesthesiology practice and education in Malaysia.\n', 'Azarinah Izaham Malaysia 022525.jpg', '+60122216141', 'speaker'),
(129, 'Varinee Lekprasert', 'varinee.lek@mahidol.ac.th', NULL, '$2y$12$kc58trsSP0rIhu0ngELwDey6uUnZTlUa.9HnA5XwGdIj3jqD7sXc.', NULL, NULL, NULL, 'cQiZMo5ezKJa63zqX150mMt4lfyFtKCnew7KxsYsKg4XLqtQEqyHn4XcsYMV', NULL, NULL, '2025-02-25 16:15:36', '2025-02-25 16:21:58', 'Varinee Lekprasert', 'Thailand', 'Ramathibodi Hospital | Thailand', '270 Rama VI Road, Thung Phaya Thai, Ractchathewi, Bangkok 10400', 'CURRICULUM VITAE\nName Varinee Lekprasert\nDate of birth April 11, 1963\nNationality Thai\nOffice address Department of Anesthesiology, Faculty of Medicine,\nRamathibodi Hospital, Bangkok 10400, Thailand\nTel : 66-02-2011513\nEducation\n1980-1984 Bachelor of Science, Faculty of Science, Chulalongkorn University, Bangkok\n1984-1986 Premedicine, Faculty of Art & Sciences, University of Toledo, Ohio, USA\n1986-1990 Doctor of Medicine, Ross University, School of Medicine, West Indies\n1998-2000 Master Degree in Epidemiology, New York Medical College, New York, USA\nPostgraduate qualification\n1992-1993 Diploma in Clinical Science (Anesthesiology)\nFaculty of Medicine, Ramathibodi Hospital\nMahidol University, Bangkok, Thailand\n1995 Diploma of Thai Board of Anesthesiology\nThe Medical Council, Thailand\n1995 Fellow of the Royal College of Anesthesiologists of\nThailand (FRCAT)\nOfficial Appointment\n1995 - 2006 Instructor\n2007-2008 Deputy director, Ramathibodi Hospital\n2009 till present Program director of Neuroanesthesia fellowship, Ramathibodi Hospital\n2012-2013 Scientific co-ordinator\nThe Royal College of Anesthesiologists of Thailand\n2014-2015 Editor-in-chief, Thai journal of Anesthesiology\nThe Royal College of Anesthesiologists of Thailand\n2015-2016 Scientific co-ordinator\nThe Royal College of Anesthesiologists of Thailand\n2016-2020 Deputy director, Ramathibodi Hospital\nChair of operating room committee\n2017-2018 Committee of Thai Board of Anesthesiology\n2004-2022 Committee of Sub-board of Neuroanesthesia\n2020-2021 Committee of the Royal College of Anesthesiologists of Thailand\n2022-present Head of department, Department of Anesthesiology\n2022-2023 President-elect, The Royal College of Anesthesiologists of Thailand\n2022-present Asian Australasian Regional Section (AARS) board member\n2022-present Board committees of Bangkok Anesthesia Regional Training Center (BARTC)\n2024-2025 President of the Royal College of Anesthesiologists of Thailand', 'Varinee Lekprasert Thailand 022525.jpg', '+66816105837', 'speaker'),
(130, 'Sanjib Adhikary', 'sadhikary1@pennstatehealth.psu.edu', NULL, '$2y$12$jpD4H1q8E6Kmpy9VvFo45ekJVct8Lqbpy7ZYcunfDFb0ft7CH8k6.', NULL, NULL, NULL, 'Z18bx8qHJXU5gZU4b3XuhBwGI4f7RnY6Ul0FDGRFSImHVb8mtCcm7M9F30Cv', NULL, NULL, '2025-02-26 05:26:26', '2025-05-26 22:49:28', 'Sanjib Adhikary', 'United States', 'Penn State College of Medicine | USA', '500,Univ.Drive, Hershey Pennsylvania', 'Dr. Sanjib Adhikary is a Professor of Anesthesiology, Orthopedics & Rehabilitation, at Penn State College of Medicine. He serves as the Division chief for Regional Anesthesia and Acute Pain Medicine at Milton S. Hershey Medical Center, at Hershey. Dr. Adhikary is also known as an outstanding educator for which he has received numerus number of awards for his teaching skills including three-time best teacher of the year voted by his trainees. For his contribution to education in 2023 he received distinguished educator award and was included into the society of distinguished educators of Penn State College of Medicine. He is not only an educator but also an innovator. For his innovation pursuit the college of medicine awarded him Investigator to watch award in 2022. This award is presented to an individual who exemplifies innovation and entrepreneurship in research through a demonstrated interest in developing new technologies, processes or services. He has been involved with the number of premier societies related to his specialty such as American Society of Regional Anesthesia, American Society of Anesthesiologists, Canadian Society of Anesthesia. He has been teaching ultrasound guided regional anesthesia techniques to American society of Anesthesiologist’s members and in Canadian Society of Anesthesiologist meeting since 2009. He has been a Visiting professor to number of esteemed institutions such as University of Virginia, Hospital for Special Surgery, University of London Ontario. He is very active in Global health initiatives propagating safe anesthesia and outreach programs in different part of the world.', 'Sanjib Adhikary USA 060225.jpg', '+1 717-829-4201', 'speaker'),
(131, 'Yong Chow Yen', 'ycyen2002@yahoo.com', NULL, '$2y$12$xAvdsod4FfaKPmxSpdTR3Oz7ZR5/Qm40bDaVFoRkb3eJwZ0hiHV5m', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, '2025-02-26 14:06:52', '2025-02-26 14:10:17', 'Yong Chow Yen', 'Malaysia', 'Lam Wha Ee Hospital, Penang | Malaysia', 'Unit 3.3, No 5, Jalan Kepimpinan P8H, Presint 8, 62250 Putrajaya, Malaysia', 'Dato’ Dr Yong Chow Yen M.D.(MAL), M. ANAES. (MAL), FRCA (UK), FAMM \nDato’ Dr Yong is the current President of the Malaysian Society of Anaesthesiologists, Malaysia. She is also a Council Member and Fellow of the College of Anaesthesiologists, Academy of Medicine of Malaysia, and a member of the Anaesthesiology and Critical Care Education Sub-Committee of the Malaysian Medical Council. She is currently a Consultant Cardiothoracic Anaesthesiologist at Lam Wah Ee and Mount Miriam Cancer Hospitals, Penang. \nShe served the Ministry of Health Malaysia from 1991-2022, during which she held various leadership roles: \n•	Head Anaesthesiology and Intensive Care Services, Penang State Health Department \n•	Chair of Parallel Pathway Specialist Training, Anaesthesiology and Critical Care, Ministry of Health, Malaysia.\n•	Program Coordinator and Examiner, Advance Diploma in Cardiovascular Healthcare (Cardiovascular Perfusion, Cardiothoracic Intensive Care Nursing), Ministry of Health, Malaysia. \n•	Deputy National Head, Cardiothoracic Anaesthesiology and Perfusion Services, Ministry of Health, Malaysia.\n\n\n', 'Yong Chow Yen Malaysia 022625.jpg', '+60124344022', 'speaker'),
(132, 'Patrick Giam', 'l.yonan@asahq.org', NULL, '$2y$12$LgZvx1VBEcN8k3AtYqBhLur8ZmJ7omEhH2eR7MJw2pTT4cVIDCxWm', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, '2025-02-27 00:21:57', '2025-02-27 00:38:05', 'Patrick Giam', 'USA', 'American Society of Anesthesiologists President', '1061 American Ln Schaumburg, IL 60173', 'Patrick Giam, M.D., FASA, is president of the American Society of Anesthesiologists (ASA), and a physician partner of U.S. Anesthesia Partners in Houston, Texas, a clinical assistant professor of Weill Cornell Medical College, an assistant professor of clinical anesthesiology at the Houston Methodist Academic Institute and an adjunct clinical assistant professor of the Texas A&M School of Medicine.\nDr. Giam is a long-time member of ASA and advocate for the specialty, Dr. Giam has served ASA in numerous roles, most recently as president-elect, first vice president and chief of the Division of Administrative Affairs. He has also been speaker of the House of Delegates and chair of the Committee on Large Group Practice. Dr. Giam is a former director of the Anesthesia Quality Institute and a former member of the Executive Board of the ASA Political Action Committee.\nHe is a long-serving member of the Texas Society of Anesthesiologists and was president in 2009. He is a member of the Texas Medical Association, the American Institute of Parliamentarians and is a registered parliamentarian of the National Association of Parliamentarians. Dr. Giam received his Bachelor of Science degree in zoology from Texas A&M University in College Station and his medical degree from Baylor College of Medicine in Houston, Texas. He completed his internship in internal medicine and his residency in anesthesiology at the Hospital of the University of Pennsylvania in Philadelphia, and his fellowship in cardiovascular anesthesiology at the Texas Heart Institute in Houston, Texas. He is board-certified in anesthesiology. ', 'Patrick Giam USA 022725.jpg', NULL, 'speaker'),
(133, 'Daniela Filipescu', '1danielaf@gmail.com', NULL, '$2y$12$5GygBZxAUbiHLUmmddprVupMcCQ5mI0T8bfc.w/Ax0vqwHk.5td7O', NULL, NULL, NULL, '4Mf1A2lAvIkYZeNPyOUqnsR5WBNeJDDOOJznEQz2bo5gCpBhls0pvdkKColt', NULL, NULL, '2025-03-02 18:37:33', '2025-03-02 18:40:10', 'Daniela Filipescu', 'Romania', 'WFSA President | Romania', 'Sos Fundeni 256-258', 'Daniela Filipescu, MD, PhD, DESA, FESAIC, is a cardiac anaesthesiologist, Professor of Anaesthesia and Intensive Care Medicine at the „Carol Davila“ University of Medicine and Pharmacy and chief of the Cardiac Anaesthesia and Intensive Care Unit II at the Emergency Institute of Cardiovascular Diseases in Bucharest, Romania. \nProfessor Filipescu is currently the President of the World Federation of Societies of Anaesthesiologists (WFSA) for the term 2024-2026. She served as President of the European Society of Anaesthesiology and Intensive Care (ESAIC)(2014-2015) and Vice-chair of the Steering Committee of the European Sepsis Alliance (2019-2022).  She is a member of the Senate and Chair of the Scientific Committee of the National Congress of the Romanian Society of Anaesthesia and Intensive Care (SRATI). \nProfessor Filipescu was awarded the ESAIC Honorary membership in 2017 and the Fellow (FESAIC) title in 2022, as a recognition of the significant contribution made to anaesthesiology and intensive care medicine.  She was also awarded the Associate Professor title at the University of Medicine and Pharmacy “Nicolae Testemițanu”, Chișinău, Republic of Moldova.\nProfessor Filipescu’s research main interests include haemostasis and transfusion, perioperative care of the cardiac patient, sepsis, workforce diversity and patient safety. She published more than 300 papers and book chapters, lectured in more than 300 national and international meetings, contributed to various international research groups and co-authored the ESAIC guidelines on the “Management of severe perioperative bleeding” and the European guideline on the “Management of bleeding and coagulopathy following major trauma“. \nProfessor Filipescu is currently co-chairing a national multidisciplinary group for the implementation of Patient Blood Management (PBM) in Romania and the WFSA perioperative PBM working group.', 'Daniela Filipescu Romania 030225.jpg', '+40744321011', 'speaker'),
(134, 'Sng Ban Leong', 'gmssbl@nus.edu.sg', NULL, '$2y$12$RyL6R1SvizRnzqob.4KoYusNnUtUHIbgpBoAaV6pB/93XK5XKs.7a', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, '2025-03-02 18:53:41', '2025-03-02 18:56:34', 'Sng Ban Leong', 'Singapore', 'KK Women\'s and Children\'s Hospital | Singapore', '100 Bukit Timah Road Singapore 229899', 'Ban Leong is the Head and Senior Consultant at the Department of Women’s Anaesthesia, Chief Data and Digital Officer and Deputy Campus Director of the Digital Integration Medical Innovation and Care Transformation Office at KK Women’s and Children’s Hospital. He is a Professor and Academic Vice Chair (Research) in the Anaesthesiology and Perioperative Sciences Academic Clinical Program and Lead Clinician Innovator Mentor in the Singhealth DukeNUS Academic Medical Centre. He is also a core faculty in the Singhealth Anaesthesiology Residency Program with interest in medical education innovation. Ban Leong is a National Level Clinician Scientist with funded research and innovation work. His academic interest includes obstetric anaesthesia and analgesia, pain and psychological vulnerability and closed loop feedback drug delivery systems.  ', 'Sng Ban Leong Singapore 030225.jpg', '6598306621', 'speaker'),
(135, 'Sasikaan Nimmaanrat', 'snimmaanrat@yahoo.com.au', NULL, '$2y$12$.ZRQ2ova5dL7vmCc3Xb6hOrgxhrPic3MHsArPDG9JBzvsVsS5xIhy', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, '2025-03-04 01:29:48', '2025-03-04 01:36:09', 'Sasikaan Nimmaanrat', 'Thailand', 'Faculty of Medicine, Prince of Songkla University | Thailand', 'Hat Yai, Songkhla', 'Dr. Sasikaan Nimmaanrat is an Associate Professor of Pain and Anesthesia at the Faculty of Medicine, Prince of Songkla University, Thailand. She is dedicated to improving pain management through patient care, education, and research.\n\nShe completed her pain fellowship training at the Pain Management Research Centre, Royal North Shore Hospital, University of Sydney, Australia, where she gained advanced skills in pain assessment and treatment. Her work focuses on all types of pain, including acute, chronic, and neuropathic pain, as well as interventional procedures to help patients manage their pain more effectively.\n\nIn addition to her academic and clinical roles, Dr. Nimmaanrat is actively involved in pain management initiatives. She is the Chair of the Pain Quality Network, working to improve pain care standards and promote best practices. She is also the Chair of the Local Arrangements Committee (LAC) for the International Association for the Study of Pain (IASP) World Congress 2026, which will be held in Bangkok, Thailand. In this role, she helps organize one of the most important global conferences on pain medicine, bringing together experts from around the world.\n\nThrough her work, Dr. Nimmaanrat strives to enhance pain treatment, educate the next generation of doctors, and contribute to advancements in pain medicine.\n', 'Sasikaan Nimmaanrat Thailand 030425.jpg', '+66887907842', 'speaker'),
(136, 'Abstract Admin', 'abstracts@aca2025manila.org', NULL, '$2y$12$BNG1ISbxIjRMFWX9l23dyOcEHvQIo1FWMvRTsQFc/DC.ptzECyUmW', NULL, NULL, NULL, 'IJuEFqohcYDBcrkMNP7j83Dg45XePl9jQ7Hs7ZOZg0v6wAvOiAUAIYottF6Q', 35, NULL, '2025-03-14 16:20:33', '2025-03-14 16:23:55', 'Abstract Admin', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 'abstract'),
(137, 'Shahridan Mohd Fathil', 'cooldoc1971@gmail.com', NULL, '$2y$12$wGk/ujIpUUxifofGAhkgNe673J.ltFS76/n.potJSFecaDO5Q.CKe', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, '2025-03-15 07:20:27', '2025-03-15 07:23:26', 'Shahridan Mohd Fathil', 'Malaysia', 'Gleneagles Hospital Johor | Malaysia', '2, Jalan Medini Utara 4, 79250 Iskandar Puteri, Johor, Malaysia ', 'Dr Shahridan Mohd Fathil obtained his MBBS from the University of Malaya in 1996. He underwent anaesthesia training initially in Malaysia, and then Ireland and England, and completed a Regional Anaesthesia Fellowship in Royal Perth Hospital, Western Australia. He was a consultant and later senior consultant with Alexandria and Ng Teng Fong General hospitals, and also a clinical senior lecturer with National University of Singapore Yoong Loo Lin School of Medicine before his move to Gleneagles Medini.\n\nHis passions are ultrasound guided regional anaesthesia and point-of-care ultrasound.\n\nHe was the past convenor for the special interest group in regional anaesthesia, College of Anaesthesiologists, Academy of Medicine, Malaysia and is the member of the executive committee for the Society of Critical and Emergency Sonography, Malaysia. \n\nHe has been on humanitarian relief work in post-natural and complex disaster missions in Indonesia, Philippines, Pakistan and recently in Gaza in 2024 with MercyMalaysia and Iraq with Médecins sans frontières in 2019.\n', 'Shahridan Mohd Fathil Malaysia 031525.jpg', '+60122949154', 'speaker');
